# Nivo78 Rule Projection — 18-web-seo-release

**Binding status:** Maintained enforcement projection of the canonical Nivo78 Product Standard.
**Source:** `reference/NIVO78_APP_STANDARD.txt`
**Authority:** Canonical standard and rule-ID catalog control if this projection differs.

## Agent instructions
- Apply whenever this scope is relevant.
- Preserve canonical rule IDs.
- Treat requirements as binding unless the canonical standard explicitly marks them `[QA]` or conditional.
- Do not weaken requirements for convenience.
- If a requirement cannot be met, stop and use the approved override process.

---

WEB SEO — COMPREHENSIVE SEARCH AND SHARING METADATA
(MANDATORY)

\================================================================================



Principle

\- Every public product web surface must be
discoverable and shareable with accurate titles and summaries.

\- SEO copy must match shipped product behavior — same
honesty rules as marketing and legal pages.

\- Any website change that adds or edits a public page
MUST include SEO review in the same pass (not a later task).



In-repo static legal HTML (code/Website/{product}/)

\- Every public HTML page (\<html
lang="en">) MUST include in \<head>:

  - Unique \<title>
(product name + page purpose; \~70 characters max)

  - meta
name="description" (plain-language summary; \~160 characters max)

  - meta
name="robots" content="index, follow" (unless a deliberate
noindex exception is documented)

  - meta
name="author" content="Nivo78 Mobile Apps, LLC"

  - link
rel="canonical" href="https\://nivo78.com/{product}/…"
(exact URL for that page)

  - Open Graph:
og\:type, og\:site\_name, og\:title, og\:description, og\:url, og\:locale

  - Twitter:
twitter\:card, twitter\:title, twitter\:description (summary or
summary\_large\_image)

\- Canonical URLs MUST match in-app support URL
registry and store listing URLs.

\- Legal pages use article or website og\:type as
appropriate; product marketing pages use website.



Hosted PHP pages (sibling Website repo — nivo78.com)

\- Product marketing and support hub pages MUST call
n78\_seo\_render\_head() from include/n78\_seo\_head.php.

\- Each product MUST have SEO profiles registered in
n78\_seo\_head.php (e.g. apa, apa\_help, apa\_help\_article)

  with title,
description, canonical\_path, robots, og\_type, and json\_ld kinds.

\- n78\_seo\_render\_head emits: title, description,
robots, author, canonical, theme-color, favicon/apple-touch-icon,

  Open Graph,
Twitter cards, and JSON-LD (@graph with Organization, WebSite, WebPage, product
SoftwareApplication when applicable).

\- FAQ JSON-LD on product pages when FAQ content exists
(apa profile uses marketing FAQ).

\- Help KB articles override
title/description/canonical per article via article.php.



When SEO is required (checklist — same pass as copy
edit)

\- New product web page or new public route → add full
SEO head (static meta or n78\_seo\_head profile).

\- Marketing, pricing, privacy, terms, or support copy
change → review title and description still accurate.

\- URL or path change → update canonical in static HTML
and n78\_seo\_head profile canonical\_path.

\- New hosted PHP shell → wire n78\_seo\_render\_head
before ship.



Automated verify (release gate)

\- tools/verify/verify-apa-website.ps1 runs WEB SEO
checks after WEB standard checks:

  - In-repo:
WEB-SEO-\* markers on index.html, privacy/, terms/, support/index.html

  - Hosted (when
sibling Website/apa exists): n78\_seo\_head.php profiles, index.php and
support/index.php render calls

\- Rule IDs: reference/NIVO78\_STANDARD\_RULE\_IDS.txt
(WEB-SEO-\* family).

\- Failures block release gate unless covered by an
active standard override with documented reason.





