WEB TECHNICAL AND RELEASE REQUIREMENTS

\================================================================================



In-repo staging

\- Maintain HTML under code/Website/{product}/ in the
product repository (for example, code/Website/{product}/).

\- Sibling Website repo hosts live nivo78.com — deploy
is separate; updocs verifies in-repo pages and exports Help KB when present.



Release verify (before ship)

\- tools/verify/verify-apa-website.ps1 (or product
equivalent) confirms required files exist and contain standard markers:

  legal.css,
site-footer, local-first / data-on-device language, support mailto, privacy
policy-product-name header, privacy and terms cross-links,

  will-do and
won’t-do section headings on product index.html, scope summary on
support/index.html,

  and
comprehensive SEO markers (meta description, canonical, Open Graph, Twitter) on
every in-repo public HTML page plus hosted n78\_seo\_head wiring,

  and WEB LEGAL
SYNC (privacy Last updated, terms effective date/version, policy-product-name
text vs engine legal copy).

\- Release gates run the applicable product website verifier for every product
that ships web pages; products without web pages do not run a website gate.

\- ApaInRepoLegalSecurityCopyTest runs in
desktopRegressionVerify — same legal sync contract as WEB LEGAL SYNC.



Updocs workflow (when copy changes)

\- Engine security/legal copy → in-repo privacy/terms/support
HTML → Website Help KB PHP → export script.

\- Run: pwsh -NoProfile -File
tools/maintain/run-updocs.ps1





\================================================================================

PRE-SHIP BAR (WEB — FAMILY CONSISTENCY)

\================================================================================



\- code/Website/{product}/ contains index.html,
privacy/, terms/, support/, legal.css before store listing.

\- Hosted URLs live at
nivo78.com/{product}/privacy|terms|support/ and match in-app support URL
registry.

\- Support page: philosophy callout, contact block
(support/feedback/contact), bug reports → in-app Feedback callout, legal links,
entity footer, will/won’t scope summary.

\- Product index: will do for you + won’t do for you
sections aligned with reference/MARKETING\_COPY.txt.

\- Privacy and terms: last updated / effective date,
cross-links, copy aligned with engine security/legal registries.

\- No web trackers or upload forms on legal/support
pages; contact is mailto-only.

\- Partner Center / store listing privacy URL equals
in-app Privacy link.

\- verify-apa-website.ps1 (or product script) green
including WEB SEO checks; Legal.txt text test run when consent or policy
changes.

\- Every public web page change includes SEO
title/description/canonical review in the same pass.



Legal gating and acknowledgement (app)

\- First-run modal with unchecked acceptance checkbox;
Accept disabled until checked; Terms and Privacy linked before accept.

\- Decline behavior matches button label on every
platform; re-consent when terms version bumps.

\- Versioned acceptance record persisted; core
workflows gated until accepted.

\- Legal.txt text test green when consent or
TERMS\_VERSION changes.





